    {
      "title": "Anthropic sets share price at $83 for stock market debut, above expected range",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/18/anthropic-share-price-stock-market-ipo",
      "description": "<p>Artificial intelligence firm positioned for one of the biggest IPOs in history, with trading slated to begin Thursday</p><p>Anthropic set the share price for its debut on the US stock market <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/anthropic-prices-initial-public-offering\">at $83</a> on Wednesday,<strong> </strong>positioning the artificial intelligence company for one of the biggest initial public offerings in history. The firm is slated to begin trading on Thursday under the ticker symbol ANT, with CEO Dario Amodei and other co-founders ringing the bell to open the Nasdaq exchange.</p><p>The pricing is above Anthropic’s earlier estimates. Last week, the San Francisco-based company, founded in 2021, set its preliminary share price at $70 to $78. With all shares counted, those prices put Anthropic’s initial public offering (IPO) from $1.26tn to $1.41tn. Elon Musk’s SpaceX debuted on Wall Street in June with the biggest market offering ever at $1.77tn. With Anthropic setting its share price at $83, it could now surpass SpaceX.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/18/anthropic-share-price-stock-market-ipo\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-18T21:39:15"
    },
